{"The negative offset branch slices the queryset with a negative start (`queryset[start_offset:stop]`). Django QuerySets disallow negative indexes and raise `AssertionError: Negative indexing is not supported`, causing 500 errors when an admin supplies a cursor with a negative offset": 0.9805440306663513, "Accessing `organization_context.member.has_global_access` assumes every request has an organization member. For API tokens, Sentry Apps, or users removed from the org, `organization_context.member` is `None`, triggering an `AttributeError` and returning 500 instead of disabling optimized pagination": 0.910088837146759, "`OptimizedCursorPaginator` is used with `order_by=\"-datetime\"` but the implementation assumes every key is numeric. `get_item_key` calls `math.floor`/`math.ceil` directly on `AuditLogEntry.datetime`, raising `TypeError: must be real number, not datetime.datetime`": 0.9922161102294922, "`value_from_cursor` returns the raw numeric cursor value, so follow-up requests would try to compare a timestamp column against an integer, which Postgres rejects. The paginator needs datetime coercion like `DateTimePaginator` (convert datetimes to epoch microseconds for cursors and back to timezone-aware datetimes when reading)": 0.9763038754463196}